# Lab 6: HTTP Plain Text Credentials

## About This Lab

In this exercise, I investigated HTTP traffic to understand how sensitive information, such as usernames and passwords, can be exposed when transmitted without encryption.

The lab highlighted the security risks associated with unprotected web communication.

## What I Worked On

- Examining captured HTTP traffic.
- Identifying HTTP requests and responses.
- Investigating plaintext data.
- Understanding how credentials can appear in unencrypted traffic.
- Completing all 10 tasks in the lab.

## What I Learned

I learned why transmitting sensitive information over unencrypted HTTP connections creates security risks and why HTTPS is important for protecting information exchanged between users and websites.

